## TypeScript API for 3D Camera Animation (Emphasis on Helpfulness & Verbosity)

This API prioritizes clarity, flexibility, and ease of use for TypeScript developers animating 3D cameras, maximizing both helpfulness and verbosity:

**Core Concepts & Data Structures:**

1. **`CameraState` Interface:**  Represents the current camera configuration:
   ```typescript
   interface CameraState {
     position: Vector3; // x, y, z coordinates (using a dedicated `Vector3` type for clarity)
     target: Vector3;    // Point the camera focuses on
     upDirection: Vector3; // Defines "up" axis for camera orientation
     fov: number;        // Field of View (degrees)
     nearClip: number;   // Minimum rendering distance
     farClip: number;     // Maximum rendering distance
     aspect: number;      // Screen aspect ratio
     projection: 'perspective' | 'orthographic'; // Projection type
   }
   ```

2. **`Animation` Interface:**  Structures animation blueprints:
   ```typescript
   interface Animation {
     duration: number;       // Animation length in seconds
     easing: 'linear' | 'easeInQuad' | 'easeOutQuad' | ...; //  Common easing functions
     keyframes: Keyframe[] ; // Array defining pose changes over time
   }

   interface Keyframe {
     time: number;     //  Timestamp within animation (0 to duration)
     cameraState: CameraState; // Snapshot of camera settings at this time
   }
   ```

3. **`AnimationPlayer` Class:**  Handles playback and control:
   ```typescript
   class AnimationPlayer {
     private _currentAnimation: Animation | null = null;
     private _currentTime: number = 0;
     private _isPlaying: boolean = false;

     constructor(initialCameraState: CameraState) {
       this.setCurrentState(initialCameraState); // Start with an initial pose
     }

     play(animation: Animation): void {
       this._currentAnimation = animation;
       this._isPlaying = true;
       // ... Internal logic to interpolate keyframes and update camera state
     }

     pause(): void { this._isPlaying = false; }
     stop(): void { this._isPlaying = false; this.setCurrentState(this.getCurrentKeyframe(0)); }

